 "verdict": [
  "clean: 0 duplicate (date,ticker) rows in the parquet; 0 rows with close<=0 or volume<0 in equity_eod.",
  "clean: no unexplained missing trading days and no low-coverage (partial-ingest) days; all 13 missing weekdays are official NSE 2025 holidays.",
  "note: the 2026 portion has no holiday closures at all (every weekday trades) -- a simulated continuous calendar; do not build calendar/seasonality features on 2026 data.",
  "regime skew: monthly median y_raw_20d swings from -8.61% (2026-02) to +5.67% (2026-03); up_5d monthly base rate ranges 0.18-0.72 -- the SECONDARY up_5d task inherits market beta, so expect fold-to-fold metric swings there; the PRIMARY beat_mkt_20d label is cross-sectionally demeaned (monthly base rate ~0.50 by construction) and is regime-robust.",
  "note: at least one month's median 20d forward return exceeds +/-3% -- economic metrics (top-decile mean fwd) on y_raw are regime-dominated; use y_excess_20d for economics, as the harness does.",
  "features >10% NaN (5): mom_12_1 (58%), ret_252d (58%), ret_126d (23%), cs_rank_ret_126 (23%), dist_200dma (21%) -- structural, not bugs: 126/252-session lookbacks cannot exist before ~Mar-2026 (DB starts Mar-2025) and deliv_pct is absent for SME/trade-to-trade segments. The harness median-imputes and ships *_isnan indicators; early CV folds see these columns mostly imputed, so treat ret_252d/mom_12_1 importances with suspicion.",
  "redundancy: 18 feature pairs with |spearman|>0.85 (momentum/SMA-distance/vol families and cs_rank twins) -- fine for trees, but collinearity will destabilize linear/NN coefficient interpretation; consider dropping one of each pair for linear models.",
  "labels: label_beat_mkt_20d NaN on 6.7% of rows (the unlabeled tail after 2026-09-15 plus short histories) -- harness drops them; y_excess_20d per-date median is exactly 0 (max abs 0.0).",
  "label cleaning: y_clean_20d masks 7.2% of rows (split/circuit/suspension-poisoned 20d windows; 0.5% of rows sit within 20d of a >22% 1-day move). Prices are UNADJUSTED (no corporate-action feed): the mask is the only defense, so never evaluate on y_clean_20d=False rows.",
  "splits: all folds populated; first fold (2026-04) trains on only 269,271 rows / 189 days vs 404,812 for the holdout -- expect the earliest fold to be the weakest and do not tune on it alone."
